From 95f9467c60da52daacebd5dfc7380f0962d05cd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:38:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(edm): wire taper by angle word - the control's
 corner rule as machine data

A wire EDM may state an angle-word taper dialect (edm.taper_angle: the
side a positive angle leans the top, and the corner rule mitre or cone,
each enumerated with no default) with edm.codes.taper_angle ({angle}).
The generator lays what the stated rule cuts - mitre is #536's path
byte for byte, cone pivots the wire about each top corner with its lean
held - so the wire laws judge the real lean and a corner the rule
gouges blocks the post. The post writes taper_on and the signed angle
word before the lead-in, X Y on the programmed (top) plane, no U/V, and
taper_off before the lead-out. An unstated rule, a machine stating
neither uv nor an angle word, and a 4-axis cut on an angle-word machine
are refused by name. U/V machines are byte-identical.

Fixes #1164

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
